1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,778
This is a ruin.

2
00:00:02,678 --> 00:00:04,854
It's a place a ship can fly inside,

3
00:00:05,304 --> 00:00:07,539
and it's older than anyone who could have built it.

4
00:00:08,439 --> 00:00:10,572
Nobody modeled it in a drawing program.

5
00:00:12,372 --> 00:00:14,859
It's this: about fifty lines of text.

6
00:00:15,759 --> 00:00:18,202
In this class, you write one of your own.

7
00:00:18,652 --> 00:00:21,327
Today, you fly one that somebody else wrote,

8
00:00:21,777 --> 00:00:23,886
and then you read how it was made.

9
00:00:25,086 --> 00:00:27,322
First, a new mission.

10
00:00:28,222 --> 00:00:30,937
This class doesn't build on the one from Class 1.

11
00:00:31,387 --> 00:00:33,803
That story ends the game ten minutes in,

12
00:00:34,253 --> 00:00:36,615
and a ruin takes longer than that to fly.

13
00:00:37,515 --> 00:00:41,828
So I make a mission the way I did in Class 1, and I call it My Ruin.

14
00:00:43,628 --> 00:00:46,186
Then I bring its libraries up to date,

15
00:00:46,636 --> 00:00:49,005
open the folder in the editor, and run lint.

16
00:00:49,905 --> 00:00:53,928
It's clean, and it's the same small mission you started Class 1 with.

17
00:00:55,128 --> 00:00:58,290
There's a shipped campaign that's built out of ruins,

18
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:01,825
and one of its smallest is called The Sink.

19
00:01:02,725 --> 00:01:06,534
It's one enormous flooded room, with a hole in one end.

20
00:01:08,334 --> 00:01:10,822
I go to the very end of my file,

21
00:01:11,272 --> 00:01:13,514
and I paste a cut-down copy of it.

22
00:01:14,414 --> 00:01:15,607
Don't read it yet.

23
00:01:16,057 --> 00:01:18,766
Just save, and run lint, and it's clean.

24
00:01:19,666 --> 00:01:23,063
One line in there isn't in the shipped file,

25
00:01:23,513 --> 00:01:26,881
and that's the line that says where the ruin stands.

26
00:01:28,081 --> 00:01:30,659
I start the game with a server and a Helm console.

27
00:01:31,559 --> 00:01:36,013
And there on the map, past the hulk and off to one side, is The Sink.

28
00:01:36,913 --> 00:01:40,894
The name sits at the mouth of the way in, so that's where I fly.

29
00:01:42,694 --> 00:01:45,655
Now I'm in the inlet, a long narrow room,

30
00:01:46,105 --> 00:01:47,260
and there's the haze.

31
00:01:48,160 --> 00:01:52,702
And here it opens out, into a room five thousand across.

32
00:01:54,502 --> 00:01:56,399
There's a mass hanging in the middle of it.

33
00:01:56,849 --> 00:01:57,737
I fly round that,

34
00:01:58,187 --> 00:01:59,579
and I'm on the far side.

35
00:02:00,479 --> 00:02:03,395
Notice the names that turned up on the map as I came near.

36
00:02:03,845 --> 00:02:06,016
Those are places, and you'll write those too.

37
00:02:07,216 --> 00:02:09,062
Now let's read it, as a list.

38
00:02:09,962 --> 00:02:12,633
It's one section, with seven records in it.

39
00:02:13,533 --> 00:02:15,888
The first record is the ruin itself.

40
00:02:16,788 --> 00:02:21,455
The next two say Box, and each of those is a room with flat sides.

41
00:02:22,355 --> 00:02:25,790
This one says Solid, and it's the mass in the middle,

42
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,549
which takes space away.

43
00:02:28,449 --> 00:02:33,303
And these three say Point, and each one is a named place.

44
00:02:35,103 --> 00:02:38,501
Now look at what every record but the first has in common.

45
00:02:38,951 --> 00:02:41,045
It says Relic, and then sink,

46
00:02:41,495 --> 00:02:43,010
which is the ruin's key.

47
00:02:43,910 --> 00:02:46,700
That's how a room says which ruin it belongs to.

48
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:50,485
And notice what isn't here.

49
00:02:50,935 --> 00:02:51,970
Nobody wrote a wall.

50
00:02:52,870 --> 00:02:55,362
The file says where the open space is,

51
00:02:55,812 --> 00:02:57,723
and the game puts rock around it.

52
00:02:58,923 --> 00:03:01,851
The shipped file is about three hundred and fifty lines,

53
00:03:02,301 --> 00:03:04,160
and I pasted fifty or so.

54
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,313
The rest is what this class teaches.

55
00:03:09,113 --> 00:03:11,062
Here, a place has a scene,

56
00:03:11,512 --> 00:03:14,023
a conversation of the kind you wrote in Class 2.

57
00:03:14,923 --> 00:03:17,918
Here, a place holds a thing the crew can find.

58
00:03:18,818 --> 00:03:22,456
This place is hidden, until somebody hears it from across the room.

59
00:03:23,356 --> 00:03:26,267
This is a small story for one member of the crew.

60
00:03:26,717 --> 00:03:30,810
And this is what the main screen shows as the ship arrives.

61
00:03:32,610 --> 00:03:34,844
Most of that isn't for the ship at all.

62
00:03:35,294 --> 00:03:37,867
It's for people who leave the ship in suits,

63
00:03:38,317 --> 00:03:40,260
and that comes late in this class.

64
00:03:41,160 --> 00:03:42,487
So I cut it,

65
00:03:42,937 --> 00:03:46,430
and the table on the page says what went and why.

66
00:03:47,630 --> 00:03:51,042
The Sink was a loan, so now I give it back.

67
00:03:51,942 --> 00:03:56,289
I select everything from the Relics heading to the end of the file,

68
00:03:56,739 --> 00:03:58,508
and I delete it.

69
00:03:59,408 --> 00:04:02,464
I save, I run lint, and it's clean.

70
00:04:04,264 --> 00:04:06,566
The file is sixty lines long again,

71
00:04:07,016 --> 00:04:09,073
and that's where the next lecture starts.

72
00:04:10,273 --> 00:04:12,417
Before you delete it, play with it.

73
00:04:13,317 --> 00:04:15,192
Change the color of the haze.

74
00:04:15,642 --> 00:04:19,463
Move the whole ruin somewhere else, and find it again.

75
00:04:20,363 --> 00:04:21,857
Make the big room smaller,

76
00:04:22,307 --> 00:04:25,173
and read what lint tells you about that.

77
00:04:26,973 --> 00:04:28,339
Then put the game away,

78
00:04:28,789 --> 00:04:31,431
and answer three questions from the file alone.

79
00:04:33,231 --> 00:04:36,067
Next time, you write a ruin of your own,

80
00:04:36,517 --> 00:04:38,051
starting from an empty page.
